%S A402098 1,183,295,583,799,943,150220,154632,188955,249968,253827,358587,
%T A402098 16541952,19237120,19723824,21450096,21477312,21489408,21494784,
%U A402098 191610880,286978140,331619184,351459648,2017198080
%N A402098 Numbers k such that psi(k) = phi(k) + Omega(k)^7.
%C A402098 The Python program available in the linked GitHub repository computes the solutions to the equation psi(k) = phi(k) + Omega(k)^m for arbitrary positive integer values of m. For this sequence, use m = 7.
%H A402098 S. I. Dimitrov, <a href="https://github.com/Stoyan16/Numbers-k-such-that-psi-k-phi-k-Omega-k-6/blob/main/A401783">Python program</a> (GitHub).
%e A402098 183 is a term since psi(183) = 248 = 120 + 2^7 = phi(183) + Omega(183)^7.
%o A402098 (PARI) isok(k) = {my(f = factor(k)); prod(i=1, #f~, (f[i, 1]+1) * f[i, 1]^(f[i, 2]-1)) - eulerphi(f) == bigomega(f)^7; } \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Nov 16 2026
%Y A402098 Cf. A000010, A001222, A001615, A401783.
%K A402098 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A402098 1,2
